Lab 2: Configuring OpenShift Virtualization
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Verify the installation and status of KubeVirt components including API server and controllers
Configure operator permissions and Security Context Constraints (SCCs) for OpenShift Virtualization
Validate proper installation and permissions for OpenShift Virtualization components
Understand the architecture and components of OpenShift Virtualization
Troubleshoot common configuration issues with OpenShift Virtualization
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of OpenShift/Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, operators)
Familiarity with command-line interface (CLI) operations
Knowledge of YAML configuration files
Understanding of Linux permissions and security contexts
Completed Lab 1: Installing OpenShift Virtualization or have OpenShift Virtualization already installed
Access to an OpenShift cluster with cluster-admin privileges
