Conclusion
In this lab, you have successfully:

Verified KubeVirt components including the API server, controllers, and handlers
Configured and validated operator permissions and Security Context Constraints
Tested the complete installation through end-to-end validation
Learned troubleshooting techniques for common configuration issues
This configuration is essential for running virtual machines on OpenShift. The KubeVirt components you verified work together to provide virtualization capabilities:

virt-api serves the KubeVirt API and handles VM lifecycle requests
virt-controller manages VM resources and ensures desired state
virt-handler runs on each node and manages VM instances locally
The proper configuration of permissions and SCCs ensures that these components can operate securely while having the necessary privileges to manage virtual machines. This foundation enables you to create, manage, and operate virtual machines alongside containerized applications in your OpenShift environment.

Understanding these components and their configuration is crucial for the Managing Virtual Machines with Red Hat OpenShift Virtualization certification and for successfully operating virtualized workloads in production environments.
